{
  "duration": 61.68,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.459,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.899,
      "end": 2.98,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.519,
      "end": 4.259,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.819,
      "end": 7.699,
      "text": "we are given that two trains are moving in opposite directions."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.199,
      "end": 11.38,
      "text": "The speed of the first train is forty-five kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.96,
      "end": 15.059,
      "text": "The speed of the second train is fifty-five kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.639,
      "end": 16.399,
      "text": "The question is"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.899,
      "end": 19.119,
      "text": "asking us to find their relative speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.6,
      "end": 23.119,
      "text": "Now, before using the formula, let us understand one simple concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.579,
      "end": 28.899,
      "text": "Relative speed tells us how fast one object is moving with respect to the other."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.359,
      "end": 32.519,
      "text": "When two trains move in the same direction, we subtract their speeds."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.88,
      "end": 34.559,
      "text": "But when they move in opposite directions,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.939,
      "end": 37.759,
      "text": "they come towards each other, so their speeds get added."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.079,
      "end": 40.559,
      "text": "This is a direct formula-based question."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.0,
      "end": 45.899,
      "text": "Relative speed is equal to the sum of both speeds. Now let us put the given values."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.299,
      "end": 54.359,
      "text": "Relative speed is equal to forty-five plus fifty-five. After adding them, we get one hundred kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.759,
      "end": 59.359,
      "text": "So the relative speed of the two trains is one hundred kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.799,
      "end": 61.68,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
